-- Tests for ea-witnesses-privilege.l4 (Evidence Act 1893, ss 120 to 136).
-- Expected values are read off the Act's text and illustrations.  Generated by generators/ea_tests_3.py.

`the Code says the notice conditions are met and sections 265 and 266 do not apply` MEANS `Code Conclusions` WITH
    `the notice requirements and other conditions prescribed under section 428 of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010 are complied with` IS TRUE
    `evidence of the fact is admissible by virtue of section 265 or 266 of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010` IS FALSE
`the Code says sections 265 or 266 make the evidence admissible` MEANS `Code Conclusions` WITH
    `the notice requirements and other conditions prescribed under section 428 of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010 are complied with` IS FALSE
    `evidence of the fact is admissible by virtue of section 265 or 266 of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010` IS TRUE

§ `120 to 122. Competence`

`s120 an ordinary witness` MEANS `Competence Facts` WITH
    `the court considers that the person is prevented from understanding the questions put or from giving rational answers by tender years, extreme old age, disease of body or mind, or another cause of the same kind` IS FALSE
    `the witness is unable to speak and gives evidence in another manner in which the witness can make it intelligible, in open court` IS FALSE
    `the kind of proceedings` IS `criminal proceedings`
    `the person is a party to the suit` IS FALSE
    `the person is the husband or wife of a party to the suit` IS FALSE
    `the person is the husband or wife of a person under criminal trial` IS FALSE
    `the person is the accused` IS FALSE
    `the evidence is on behalf of the accused or a person jointly charged with the accused` IS FALSE

