§ `122(4) to (8). Questions to the accused in cross-examination`

`s122(4) other offence` MEANS `Accused Cross-examination Facts` WITH
    `the accused gives evidence in the criminal proceedings` IS TRUE
    `the question tends to reveal that the accused has committed, or has been charged with or convicted or acquitted of, an offence other than the offence charged` IS TRUE
    `the question tends to reveal that the accused is generally or in a particular respect a person of bad disposition or reputation` IS FALSE
    `evidence of the fact is admissible for proving the commission of the offence charged by virtue of section 14 or 15 of the Evidence Act 1893 or another written law` IS FALSE
    `2 or more persons are jointly charged and the evidence of the fact is admissible for the purpose of showing another of the accused to be not guilty` IS FALSE
    `the accused personally or by an advocate asked a witness for the prosecution or for a person jointly charged a question concerning the witness's conduct on an occasion or whether the witness has committed, or been charged with, convicted or acquitted of, an offence` IS FALSE
    `the court is of the opinion that the main purpose of that question was to raise an issue as to the witness's credibility` IS FALSE
    `the court is of the opinion that the question is relevant to the accused's credibility as a witness` IS FALSE
    `the accused has given evidence against a person jointly charged in the same proceedings` IS FALSE
    `the party cross-examining is entitled under section 56 to establish that the accused is a person of bad disposition or reputation` IS FALSE

