§ `123 to 133. Privileges`

`s123 ill c a Judge examined as to what occurred` MEANS `Privilege Facts` WITH
    `the kind of privilege` IS `Judges and Magistrates (section 123)`
    `the witness is a Judge` IS FALSE
    `the question is as to the witness's own conduct in court as a Judge or Magistrate, or as to anything that came to the witness's knowledge in court as such` IS FALSE
    `the witness is a Magistrate and the General Division of the High Court has made a special order` IS FALSE
    `the communication was made to the witness during marriage by a person to whom the witness is or has been married` IS FALSE
    `the person who made it, or that person's representative in interest, consents to disclosure` IS FALSE
    `the proceedings are a suit between married persons or proceedings in which one married person is prosecuted for a crime committed against the other` IS FALSE
    `the evidence is of unpublished official records relating to affairs of State, or evidence derived from them` IS FALSE
    `the officer at the head of the Department concerned has given permission` IS FALSE
    `the witness is a public officer, or a member, officer or employee of, or a person seconded to, an organisation specified in the Schedule to the Official Secrets Act 1935` IS FALSE
    `the communication was made to the witness in official confidence` IS FALSE
    `the witness considers that the public interest would suffer by the disclosure` IS FALSE
    `the witness is a Magistrate or police officer, or a revenue officer asked about an offence against the public revenue or the excise laws` IS FALSE
    `the question is from where the witness got information as to the commission of an offence` IS FALSE
    `the communication was made to the advocate or solicitor, or legal counsel, in the course and for the purpose of the employment` IS FALSE
    `the document became known to the advocate or solicitor, or legal counsel, in the course and for the purpose of the employment` IS FALSE
    `the advice was given to the client, or entity, in the course and for the purpose of the employment` IS FALSE
    `the client, or entity, has given express consent` IS FALSE
    `the communication was made in furtherance of an illegal purpose` IS FALSE
    `the fact was observed in the course of the employment and shows that a crime or fraud has been committed since the commencement of the employment` IS FALSE
    `the communication to the legal counsel was not made for the purpose of seeking legal advice` IS FALSE
    `the document became known to the legal counsel otherwise than in the course of and for the purpose of seeking legal advice` IS FALSE
    `the witness is an interpreter or other person working under the supervision of a legal professional adviser` IS FALSE
    `the party gave evidence in the suit` IS FALSE
    `the party called the advocate or solicitor, or legal counsel, as a witness and questioned the witness on matters that but for the question the witness would not be at liberty to disclose` IS FALSE
    `the communication was a confidential communication between the person and the person's legal professional adviser` IS FALSE
    `the person offers himself or herself as a witness` IS FALSE
    `the communication appears to the court necessary to be known in order to explain evidence the person has given` IS FALSE
    `the witness is not a party to the suit` IS FALSE
    `the document is the witness's title deed to property, or a document by virtue of which the witness holds property as pledgee or mortgagee, or a document the production of which might tend to criminate the witness` IS FALSE
    `the witness has agreed in writing to produce it with the person seeking production or some person through whom the witness claims` IS FALSE
    `the witness is a party to the suit and the document is not relevant or material to the case of the party requiring its production` IS FALSE
    `the witness is a bank, the proceeding is one to which the bank is not a party, and the books of the bank are sought other than as provided by section 174` IS FALSE
    `the document is in the witness's possession and another person would be entitled to refuse to produce it if it were in that person's possession` IS FALSE
    `the document is produced for the purpose of identification` IS FALSE
    `that other person consents to its production` IS FALSE

`s123 ill a a Magistrate asked about conduct in court, no order` MEANS `Privilege Facts` WITH
    `the kind of privilege` IS `Judges and Magistrates (section 123)`
