    `the proceedings are a suit between married persons or proceedings in which one married person is prosecuted for a crime committed against the other` IS FALSE
    `the evidence is of unpublished official records relating to affairs of State, or evidence derived from them` IS FALSE
    `the officer at the head of the Department concerned has given permission` IS FALSE
    `the witness is a public officer, or a member, officer or employee of, or a person seconded to, an organisation specified in the Schedule to the Official Secrets Act 1935` IS FALSE
    `the communication was made to the witness in official confidence` IS FALSE
    `the witness considers that the public interest would suffer by the disclosure` IS FALSE
    `the witness is a Magistrate or police officer, or a revenue officer asked about an offence against the public revenue or the excise laws` IS FALSE
    `the question is from where the witness got information as to the commission of an offence` IS FALSE
    `the communication was made to the advocate or solicitor, or legal counsel, in the course and for the purpose of the employment` IS FALSE
