§ `134. Self-incrimination`

`s134(1) a witness whose answer would incriminate` MEANS `Self-incrimination Facts` WITH
    `the question is as to a matter relevant to the matter in issue in a suit or in a civil or criminal proceeding` IS TRUE
    `the answer will or may tend, directly or indirectly, to criminate the witness, expose the witness to a penalty or forfeiture, or establish that the witness owes a debt or is subject to a civil suit` IS TRUE
    `the witness is the accused giving evidence in criminal proceedings` IS FALSE
    `the answer would tend to prove the commission by the accused of the offence charged` IS FALSE
    `the question, document or thing is in the opinion of the court relevant solely or mainly to the accused's credibility as a witness` IS FALSE
    `the question is one asked by virtue of section 56` IS FALSE
    `the answer would tend to expose the accused to proceedings for some other offence or for the recovery of a penalty` IS FALSE
    `the answer would tend to expose the accused's wife or husband to proceedings for an offence or for the recovery of a penalty` IS FALSE
    `the witness is the wife or husband of the accused giving evidence in criminal proceedings` IS FALSE
    `the answer would tend to expose the witness to proceedings as mentioned in section 134(4)(b)(i)` IS FALSE
    `the court has explained to the witness the purport of section 134(2)` IS FALSE
    `the witness was compelled by the court to give the answer` IS FALSE
    `the proceeding is a prosecution for giving false evidence by that answer` IS FALSE

`s134(1) an irrelevant question` MEANS `Self-incrimination Facts` WITH
    `the question is as to a matter relevant to the matter in issue in a suit or in a civil or criminal proceeding` IS FALSE
